    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I have a practical but not deeply theoretical relationship with math. As a biology and chemistry enthusiast, I use it for problem-solving in science but avoid abstract concepts. My upper secondary education gave me foundational skills, and I appreciate its role in real-world applications like data analysis in my volunteering work.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "I rarely feel anxious about math because I focus on practical applications. My high conscientiousness helps me stay organized when tackling problems, and my low agreeableness means I don’t overemphasize social pressure. Anxiety usually arises only when math feels disconnected from real-life contexts.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used AI tools like Wolfram Alpha to verify my chemistry calculations and solve basic algebra problems. It helped me quickly check my work and understand steps I missed. I found it efficient but not a replacement for deep conceptual learning.",
